### 2.4 Tiered Licensing: Seat-Based, Metered Quota, and Enterprise Floating Licenses

Commercial agents deploy three primary enterprise licensing models:

| Licensing Topology | Allocation Mechanism | Quota Enforcement Strategy | Ideal Business Application |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Seat-Based Monthly Subscription** | 1 License Key per Named User | Single active device/session lock in Redis | Professional tools (Financial analysts, lawyers, designers) |
| **Metered Usage Quota (Credits)** | Prepaid token bucket (e.g., 500 reports/mo) | Decrement counter via atomic Redis `DECRBY` | High-compute tasks (Video rendering, deep code refactoring) |
| **Enterprise Floating Pool** | Shared organizational API Key / Domain Match | Concurrent session limit (e.g., 20 simultaneous users) | Internal enterprise departmental GPTs, corporate site licenses |

